# Interceptor's picture in the README: a chase at sunset on a road through
# the trees of the hills, full screen. Regenerate it with
#
#   cargo orchestration script documentation/interceptor.vts --resolution 1920x1200
#
# which writes documentation/images/interceptor.png at 1920x1200; scale it
# to 1280x800, the size of the other screenshots, so that the README's table
# shows them all alike (the website's pictures come from the same
# 1920x1200 shot). The game starts with the system; F3 twice turns the
# statistics off, and a quick chase at sunset is chosen from the menus (its
# menu opens on its start button; four up is the time of day, one left
# from night is sunset). The computer takes the wheel during the
# countdown, so every run films the same chase: 9 s on, the police car
# among the traffic between the trees, the sun low.
boot-cmdline "run=interceptor"
fail-on "PANIC"
fail-on "rendering stops"
wait-serial "interceptor: ready" 120
wait 2
key f3
wait 1
key f3
wait 1
key ret
wait-serial "screen Main" 10
key down
key ret
wait-serial "screen Quick" 10
key up
key up
key up
key up
key left
key down
key down
key down
key down
key ret
wait-serial "screen Playing" 10
key f8
wait-serial "autopilot on" 10
wait 9
shot documentation/images/interceptor.png now
